NO ERROR HANDLING
================================================================================

fetch(url)
  .then(
    response =>
      response.json()
  )
  .then(
    setData
  )


Problems:

• Rejection not handled

• HTTP status not checked


================================================================================
WRONG WAY 6:
LOADING ONLY STOPS ON SUCCESS
================================================================================

setLoading(
  true
)


try {

  // request

  setLoading(
    false
  )


} catch (error) {

  setError(
    error.message
  )
}


Problem:

failure path can leave:

loading = true


================================================================================
COMPARISON TABLE
================================================================================

+--------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
| WRONG PATTERN            | REAL PROBLEM                              |
+--------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
| Fetch in render          | Impure render/repeated requests           |
| Effect every render      | Repeated synchronization                  |
| Unstable dependency      | Excess Effect executions                  |
| Effect → dependency loop | Infinite state/effect cycle               |
| No obsolete control      | Race/stale results                        |
| No rejection handling    | Failed asynchronous workflow              |
| No response.ok check     | HTTP errors treated incorrectly           |
| Loading only on success  | Stuck loading state                       |
+--------------------------+-------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
PART 9: IDENTIFYING WRONG WAYS IN YOUR CODE
================================================================================

RED FLAG 1:
REPEATED NETWORK REQUESTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Open:

Browser DevTools
 ↓
Network


If you see:

GET /api/groceries

GET /api/groceries

GET /api/groceries

GET /api/groceries

GET /api/groceries


in rapid succession, investigate:

• Fetch inside render

• Effect without intended dependencies

• Effect/setState loop

• Unstable dependencies


================================================================================
RED FLAG 2:
LOADING NEVER FINISHES
================================================================================

UI:

Loading...

Loading...

Loading...


Possible causes:

• Request rejected

• Error path didn't clear loading

• Response parsing failed

• Backend never completed

• Request logic repeatedly restarts


Do NOT assume:

"infinite fetch loop"


without checking actual network activity.


================================================================================
RED FLAG 3:
OLD DATA APPEARS
================================================================================

Example:

Select User 1

then quickly:

Select User 2


UI briefly shows User 2

then suddenly:

User 1


Likely problem:

REQUEST RACE


Investigate obsolete request handling.


================================================================================
RED FLAG 4:
Uncaught (in promise)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Console:

Uncaught (in promise)


Likely:

Rejected Promise wasn't handled somewhere.


Investigate:

try/catch

or:

.catch()


================================================================================
RED FLAG 5:
404/500 PRODUCES STRANGE DATA ERROR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Possible problem:

response.ok

was never checked.


Backend returned:

500


Code tried:

response.json()


and continued as though the request were successful.


================================================================================
RED FLAG 6:
EFFECT RUNS MORE THAN EXPECTED
================================================================================

Check:

• Effect dependencies

• Objects/functions created during render

• State updated by the Effect

• Development Strict Mode behavior


Do not immediately remove dependencies to silence the issue.


================================================================================
RED FLAG 7:
DUPLICATE DEVELOPMENT FETCHES
================================================================================

If development logs show more Effect setup than expected:

Check whether:

StrictMode


is enabled before concluding that there is an infinite loop.


But your Effect should still be safe under:

setup
 ↓
cleanup
 ↓
setup


================================================================================
DEBUGGING WORKFLOW
================================================================================

STEP 1:

Open Console.


Check:

• Runtime errors

• Promise errors

• Request errors


STEP 2:

Open Network tab.


Check:

• Request count

• Request URL

• Method

• Status

• Duration

• Response


STEP 3:

Inspect dependencies.


Ask:

What reactive values does the Effect read?


STEP 4:

Check whether Effect updates state.


Ask:

Does that state change an Effect dependency again?


STEP 5:

Check object/function dependencies.


Ask:

Is this value recreated on every render?


STEP 6:

Check HTTP handling.


Look for:

response.ok


STEP 7:

Check rejection handling.


Look for:

try/catch

or:

.catch()


STEP 8:

Check obsolete requests.


Look for:

AbortController

or another stale-response strategy.


STEP 9:

Check loading paths.


Make sure loading ends after:

• Success

• Failure

and behaves sensibly after:

• Cancellation


================================================================================
DEBUGGING TABLE
================================================================================

+--------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
| SYMPTOM                  | INVESTIGATE                               |
+--------------------------+-------------------------------------------+
| Repeated requests        | Render fetch / Effect dependencies        |
| Loading forever          | Error/loading paths                       |
| Wrong user/data shown    | Race condition                            |
| Uncaught Promise         | Missing error handling                    |
| 404 treated as data      | Missing response.ok                       |
| Effect constantly runs   | Dependency identity/state loop            |
| Duplicate dev setup      | Strict Mode + cleanup correctness         |
+--------------------------+-------------------------------------------+


