================================================================================
CRITICAL CORRECTIONS TO REMEMBER
================================================================================

WRONG IDEA:

"Never use useEffect without a dependency array."


BETTER:

An Effect without a dependency array runs after every committed render.

Use it only when that behavior is actually required.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WRONG IDEA:

"Any object in the dependency array causes a loop."


BETTER:

A state object remains its current reference until state changes.

An object newly created during rendering gets a new reference each render.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WRONG IDEA:

"Every fetch without cleanup is automatically a memory leak."


BETTER:

Cancellation is especially useful for obsolete requests, race prevention,
and avoiding unnecessary network work.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WRONG IDEA:

"A rerender means the component unmounted."


BETTER:

A component can rerender many times while remaining mounted.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WRONG IDEA:

"fetch rejects for every HTTP error."


BETTER:

Check:

response.ok


for HTTP status errors.


