KEY TAKEAWAY
================================================================================

Most broken data-fetching code comes from one of three areas:

1. WRONG PLACE

   Example:
   fetch during render


2. WRONG TRIGGER

   Example:
   Effect runs repeatedly because its dependency keeps changing


3. WRONG ASYNC HANDLING

   Example:
   stale response, missing error handling, or stuck loading state


The debugging model is:

WHEN DID THE REQUEST START?
        ↓
WHY DID THE EFFECT RUN?
        ↓
WHAT DEPENDENCY CHANGED?
        ↓
DID THE REQUEST SUCCEED?
        ↓
IS THIS RESPONSE STILL CURRENT?
        ↓
DID THE UI HANDLE SUCCESS/ERROR/CANCELLATION?


Once those questions are clear, most React data-fetching problems become much
easier to diagnose.


